  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/nta_abhyas/jee_main/images/a790267b-7bb7-4d21-b2a5-1836b9f3ebd3.png\" style=\"max-width:100%; object-fit:contain\" style=\"width:2.3in;height:1.32708in\" /></p><p>Let,&nbsp;<math><mi>A</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mi></mi><mi>b</mi></mrow></mfenced></math> and <math><mi>G</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>,</mo><mi></mi><mi>k</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>.</mo></math></p><p>Now,&nbsp;<math><mi>A</mi><mo>,</mo><mi></mi><mi>G</mi><mo>,</mo><mi></mi><mi>O</mi></math> are collinear</p><p><math><mo>⇒</mo><mi>h</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>2.0</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>⇒</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn><mi>h</mi></math> and similarily <math><mi>b</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn><mi>k</mi><mo>.</mo></math><br />Now,&nbsp;<math><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mi></mi><mi>b</mi></mrow></mfenced></math> lies on the circle <math><msup><mrow><mi>x</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mrow><mi>y</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>9</mn><mo>⇒</mo><msup><mrow><mi>a</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mrow><mi>b</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></math></p><p>Hence, locus of the centroid is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></math></p>",
